# Tests for the Cdcc module (child and dependent care credit, Form 2441)

Run with `clerk test`. Each named scope is one concrete case, worked by hand
from IRC 21, IRC 129, Form 2441 (`f2441--2024.pdf`) and its instructions as
quoted in `catala/cdcc.catala_en`. Every scope sets satisfiable inputs and
asserts the expected result; most also assert that a known-bad output is not
produced. Oracle comparison: `make difftest SCOPE=cdcc`.

> Using Types
> Using Qualifying_child as Q
> Using Qualifying_relative as R
> Using Dependents_benefit_split as B
> Using Cdcc as C

## Helper: one return

The default is a head of household (born 1985-06-15) with wages of $45,000, one
qualifying child, a 4-year-old son (born 2020-03-01, claimed, SSN) with $3,000
of qualified expenses paid to a qualified provider, AGI $15,000 and a tax
liability limit of $5,000. A test overrides only what it tests.

```catala
declaration scope Case:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context child_date_of_birth content date
  context child_expenses content money
  context child_unable_to_care content boolean
  context second_child content boolean
  context second_child_expenses content money
  context agi content money
  context tax_limit content money
  context primary_wages content money
  context secondary_wages content money
  context primary_benefits content money
  context secondary_benefits content money
  context primary_plan_max content money
  context secondary_plan_max content money
  context line16 content money
  context carryover content money
  context forfeited content money
  context secondary_months content list of money
  context secondary_disabled content boolean
  context secondary_expenses content money
  context spouse_same_abode condition
  context primary_combat_pay content money
  context primary_elects_combat_for_credit content boolean
  context household_employee condition
  output f scope C.Form2441

declaration scope MkChild:
  context date_of_birth content date
  context expenses content money
  context unable content boolean
  output child content C.CdccMember

scope MkChild:
  definition child equals C.CdccMember {
    -- member: R.Member {
      -- person: Q.Person {
           -- relationship: Q.Relationship.BiologicalChild
           -- date_of_birth: date_of_birth
           -- full_time_student: false
           -- permanent_total_disability: false
           -- residency_duration: Q.ResidencyDuration.AllYear
           -- own_support: false
           -- married: false
           -- writable_joint_return: false
           -- writable_required_to_file: false
           -- writable_filing_only_for_refund: false
           -- writable_could_be_qualifying_child_of_another: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_must_file: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_did_file: false
           -- writable_potential_claimer_filed_only_for_refund: false }
      -- answers: R.DependentAnswers {
           -- gross_income: $0
           -- writable_qr_support_test: true
           -- tin_type: R.TinType.Ssn
           -- is_us_citizen_full_year: true
           -- writable_us_resident: false
           -- writable_us_national: false
           -- writable_canada_mexico_resident: false
           -- tp_claims: true }
      -- split: B.BenefitSplitAnswers {
           -- has_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent: false
           -- non_parental_some_parent_not_claiming: false
           -- which_parent_not_claiming: B.WrittenDeclaration.NobodyDid
           -- in_parents_custody: false
           -- lived_with_tp_or_other_biological_or_adoptive_parent_more_than_six_months:
                false
           -- biological_or_adoptive_parents_living: false
           -- nights_with_tp_vs_other_parent: B.NightsComparison.Less
           -- tp_agi_higher_than_other_parent: false
           -- parents_meet_reqs_rule_for_children_of_divorced_parents: false
           -- special_rule_child_used_by_custodial_parent_as_qp: false
           -- special_rule_agi_test: false
           -- parental_situation: B.ParentalSituation.Other
           -- parental_support: false
           -- multiple_support_agreement: false } }
    -- cdcc: C.CdccAnswers {
         -- unable_to_care_for_self: unable
         -- has_dependent_care_expenses: expenses > $0
         -- expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider: true
         -- writable_qualifying_expense_amount: expenses
         -- tp_paid_most_of_home_upkeep: true } }

declaration scope MkFiler:
  context wages content money
  context benefits content money
  context plan_max content money
  context months content list of money
  context disabled content boolean
  context expenses content money
  context combat content money
  context elect_credit content boolean
  output filer content C.CdccFiler

scope MkFiler:
  definition filer equals C.CdccFiler {
    -- employer_income_subtotal_base: wages
    -- nontaxable_combat_pay: combat
    -- elect_combat_pay_for_credit: elect_credit
    -- elect_combat_pay_for_benefits: false
    -- dependent_care_benefits: benefits
    -- dependent_care_plan_maximum: plan_max
    -- is_disabled: disabled
    -- deemed_income_month_earnings: months
    -- has_dependent_care_expenses: expenses > $0
    -- expenses_paid_to_qualifying_provider: true
    -- writable_qualifying_expense_amount: expenses }

scope Case:
  definition filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.HeadOfHousehold
  definition child_date_of_birth equals |2020-03-01|
  definition child_expenses equals $3,000
  definition child_unable_to_care equals false
  definition second_child equals false
  definition second_child_expenses equals $0
  definition agi equals $15,000
  definition tax_limit equals $5,000
  definition primary_wages equals $45,000
  definition secondary_wages equals $0
  definition primary_benefits equals $0
  definition secondary_benefits equals $0
  definition primary_plan_max equals $0
  definition secondary_plan_max equals $0
  definition line16 equals $0
  definition carryover equals $0
  definition forfeited equals $0
  definition secondary_months equals []
  definition secondary_disabled equals false
  definition secondary_expenses equals $0
  definition spouse_same_abode equals false
  definition primary_combat_pay equals $0
  definition primary_elects_combat_for_credit equals false
  definition household_employee equals false

  definition f.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition f.household equals
    (if second_child
     then [ (output of MkChild with { -- date_of_birth: child_date_of_birth
                                     -- expenses: child_expenses
                                     -- unable: child_unable_to_care }).child;
            (output of MkChild with { -- date_of_birth: |2018-05-05|
                                     -- expenses: second_child_expenses
                                     -- unable: false }).child ]
     else [ (output of MkChild with { -- date_of_birth: child_date_of_birth
                                     -- expenses: child_expenses
                                     -- unable: child_unable_to_care }).child ])
  definition f.minimum_filer_date_of_birth equals |1985-06-15|
  definition f.treat_filers_as_dependents equals false
  definition f.either_filer_us_citizen_or_national equals true
  definition f.treat_as_mfj equals
    filing_status = Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition f.lived_apart_last_six_months equals false
  definition f.spouse_same_abode_more_than_half_year equals spouse_same_abode
  definition f.primary_filer equals
    (output of MkFiler with { -- wages: primary_wages
                              -- benefits: primary_benefits
                              -- plan_max: primary_plan_max
                              -- months: []
                              -- disabled: false
                              -- expenses: $0
                              -- combat: primary_combat_pay
                              -- elect_credit: primary_elects_combat_for_credit }).filer
  definition f.secondary_filer equals
    (output of MkFiler with { -- wages: secondary_wages
                              -- benefits: secondary_benefits
                              -- plan_max: secondary_plan_max
                              -- months: secondary_months
                              -- disabled: secondary_disabled
                              -- expenses: secondary_expenses
                              -- combat: $0
                              -- elect_credit: false }).filer
  definition f.has_mfs_spouse_earned_income equals false
  definition f.writable_mfs_spouse_earned_income equals $0
  definition f.writable_total_qualified_dependent_care_expenses equals line16
  definition f.writable_carryover_amount equals carryover
  definition f.writable_forfeited_amount equals forfeited
  definition f.has_credit_for_prior_year_expenses equals false
  definition f.claimed_credit_for_prior_year_expenses equals false
  definition f.claimed_max_credit_for_prior_tax_year equals false
  definition f.has_household_employee equals household_employee
  definition f.benefits_from_sole_proprietorship_or_partnership equals false
  definition f.agi equals agi
  definition f.total_tentative_tax equals tax_limit
```

## Issue #28 cases

### One qualifying person, $3,000, AGI $15,000: 35 percent, $1,050

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestOneQpAgi15k:
  c scope Case

scope TestOneQpAgi15k:
  assertion c.f.benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons = 1
  assertion c.f.line3 = $3,000
  assertion c.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.35
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $1,050
  # Known-bad: 34 percent is the next band, over $15,000
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit != $1,020
  assertion not c.f.unsupported
```

### AGI $43,001: 20 percent, $600

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAgi43001:
  c scope Case

scope TestAgi43001:
  definition c.agi equals $43,001
  assertion c.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.20
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $600
```

### AGI $43,000 is still 21 percent; $15,001 and $17,001 step down

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestPercentageSteps:
  a scope Case
  b scope Case
  d scope Case
  e scope Case

scope TestPercentageSteps:
  definition a.agi equals $43,000
  definition b.agi equals $15,001
  definition d.agi equals $17,000
  definition e.agi equals $17,001
  assertion a.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.21
  assertion b.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.34
  assertion d.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.34
  assertion e.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.33
```

### Negative AGI: 35 percent (IRC 21(a)(2); DF-BUG(24))

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestNegativeAgi:
  c scope Case

scope TestNegativeAgi:
  definition c.agi equals -$500
  assertion c.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.35
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $1,050
```

### Two qualifying persons, $6,000 of expenses, AGI $30,000

AGI $30,000 is over $29,000 and not over $31,000: .27. $6,000 x .27 = $1,620.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTwoQps:
  c scope Case

scope TestTwoQps:
  definition c.second_child equals true
  definition c.child_expenses equals $3,500
  definition c.second_child_expenses equals $4,000
  definition c.agi equals $30,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons = 2
  assertion c.f.benefits.uncapped_qualifying_expenses = $7,500
  assertion c.f.line3 = $6,000
  assertion c.f.line8_decimal_amount = $0.27
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $1,620
  # Known-bad: the one-person cap
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit != $810
```

### Earned income below the expenses

The only earner makes $2,000: line 6 is $2,000, credit 20 percent = $400.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestEarnedIncomeLimit:
  c scope Case

scope TestEarnedIncomeLimit:
  definition c.primary_wages equals $2,000
  definition c.agi equals $45,000
  assertion c.f.line6 = $2,000
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $400
```

### MFJ, spouse a student for 9 months, no earnings: deemed $250 a month

Reg. 1.21-2(c) Example 2 (with 2024 amounts): one qualifying person,
$250 x 9 = $2,250 of deemed income for the spouse; the primary earns $40,000,
$5,000 of expenses; line 5 is $2,250, line 6 is $2,250; AGI $45,000 gives 20
percent, $450.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestStudentSpouse:
  c scope Case

scope TestStudentSpouse:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.primary_wages equals $40,000
  definition c.child_expenses equals $5,000
  definition c.agi equals $45,000
  definition c.secondary_months equals
    [$0; $0; $0; $0; $0; $0; $0; $0; $0]
  assertion c.f.benefits.deemed_monthly_income = $250
  assertion c.f.line5_earned_income = $2,250
  assertion c.f.line6 = $2,250
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $450
  assertion not c.f.unsupported
```

### The higher of deemed and actual income counts each month

Two months of $100 actual and one of $1,000: 150 + 150 + 1,000 = $1,300.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDeemedHigher:
  c scope Case

scope TestDeemedHigher:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.secondary_months equals [$100; $100; $1,000]
  assertion c.f.benefits.secondary_deemed_uplift = $300
  assertion c.f.line5_earned_income = $300
```

### Employer benefits of $5,000 reduce the cap to 0: credit $0

Part III: $5,000 of box 10 benefits, plan maximum $5,000, expenses $5,000.
Line 20 = $5,000, line 21 = $5,000, line 25 = $5,000, line 27 = $3,000, line 29
= -$2,000: no credit. Taxable benefits $0.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBenefits5000:
  c scope Case

scope TestBenefits5000:
  definition c.primary_benefits equals $5,000
  definition c.primary_plan_max equals $5,000
  definition c.line16 equals $5,000
  definition c.child_expenses equals $5,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.line25_excluded_benefits = $5,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.line29_net_allowable = -$2,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.taxable_benefits = $0
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $0
  # Known-bad: ignoring the exclusion would give 20 percent of $3,000 (AGI $15,000: $1,050)
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit != $1,050
```

### Benefits above the exclusion limit are taxable

$6,000 of box 10 benefits with a plan maximum of $6,000, expenses $6,000: the
exclusion is capped at $5,000 (IRC 129(a)(2)(A)); line 26 is $1,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTaxableBenefits:
  c scope Case

scope TestTaxableBenefits:
  definition c.primary_benefits equals $6,000
  definition c.primary_plan_max equals $6,000
  definition c.line16 equals $6,000
  definition c.child_expenses equals $6,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.line21_specified_exclusion = $5,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.line25_excluded_benefits = $5,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.taxable_benefits = $1,000
```

### Benefits without expenses are all taxable

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBenefitsNoExpenses:
  c scope Case

scope TestBenefitsNoExpenses:
  definition c.primary_benefits equals $560
  definition c.primary_plan_max equals $5,000
  definition c.line16 equals $0
  definition c.child_expenses equals $0
  assertion c.f.benefits.taxable_benefits = $560
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $0
```

### Benefits of $1,300 reduce the cap by $1,300

Qualifying person with $20,000 of expenses (line 16), benefits $1,300: line 25
= $1,300, line 29 = $1,700, line 31 = $1,700 (one person), credit at 20
percent = $340.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestBenefitsReduceCap:
  c scope Case

scope TestBenefitsReduceCap:
  definition c.primary_benefits equals $1,000
  definition c.carryover equals $300
  definition c.primary_plan_max equals $2,000
  definition c.line16 equals $20,000
  definition c.child_expenses equals $20,000
  definition c.agi equals $45,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.line15_adjusted_benefits = $1,300
  assertion c.f.benefits.line25_excluded_benefits = $1,300
  assertion c.f.benefits.line31 = $1,700
  assertion c.f.line3 = $1,700
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $340
```

### The tax liability limit

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestTaxLimit:
  c scope Case

scope TestTaxLimit:
  definition c.tax_limit equals $300
  assertion c.f.line9c = $1,050
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $300
```

### Child turning 13 and over 13

A child born 2011-06-01 turned 13 in 2024 and is a qualifying person for the
part of the year under 13; one born 2011-01-01 was already 13 on January 1;
one unable to care for self qualifies at any age.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestAge13:
  turned scope Case
  already scope Case
  disabled scope Case

scope TestAge13:
  definition turned.child_date_of_birth equals |2011-06-01|
  definition already.child_date_of_birth equals |2011-01-01|
  definition disabled.child_date_of_birth equals |2011-01-01|
  definition disabled.child_unable_to_care equals true
  assertion turned.f.benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons = 1
  assertion already.f.benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons = 0
  assertion already.f.cdcc_total_credit = $0
  assertion disabled.f.benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons = 1
```

### A disabled spouse is a qualifying person

MFJ, the secondary filer incapable of self care and living with the primary
all year: the filers are two qualifying persons with the child, the cap is
$6,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestDisabledSpouse:
  c scope Case

scope TestDisabledSpouse:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingJointly
  definition c.secondary_disabled equals true
  definition c.spouse_same_abode equals true
  definition c.secondary_wages equals $3,000
  definition c.secondary_expenses equals $4,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons = 2
  assertion c.f.benefits.qualifying_expense_cap = $6,000
  assertion c.f.benefits.uncapped_qualifying_expenses = $7,000
  assertion c.f.line3 = $6,000
  assertion c.f.line6 = $3,000
  # AGI $15,000: 35 percent of $3,000
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $1,050
```

### Married filing separately: no credit (IRC 21(e)(2))

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestMfs:
  c scope Case

scope TestMfs:
  definition c.filing_status equals Types.FilingStatus.MarriedFilingSeparately
  assertion c.f.benefits.married_separate_not_allowed
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $0
```

### Combat pay election

Wages $1,000, combat pay $2,500 elected: earned income $3,500, line 6 $3,000.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestCombatPay:
  elected scope Case
  not_elected scope Case

scope TestCombatPay:
  definition elected.primary_wages equals $1,000
  definition elected.primary_combat_pay equals $2,500
  definition elected.primary_elects_combat_for_credit equals true
  definition not_elected.primary_wages equals $1,000
  definition not_elected.primary_combat_pay equals $2,500
  assertion elected.f.line6 = $3,000
  assertion not_elected.f.line6 = $1,000
```

### Knockouts

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestKnockouts:
  c scope Case

scope TestKnockouts:
  definition c.household_employee equals true
  assertion c.f.unsupported
  assertion c.f.benefits.ko_knockout_household_employee
```

### Known-bad person: a 13-year-old is not a qualifying person

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestRejectsOldChild:
  c scope Case

scope TestRejectsOldChild:
  definition c.child_date_of_birth equals |2008-01-01|
  assertion not (c.f.benefits.count_of_qualifying_persons = 1)
  assertion c.f.cdcc_total_credit = $0
```
